 "title": "Fix average() dividing by one less than the number of values",
 "shortDescription": "Fix a bug in the public repository signerless/agenc-e2e-sandbox.",
 "fullDescription": "average() in src/stats.js divides the sum by values.length - 1, so average([2, 4, 6]) returns 6 instead of 4. Divide by values.length, keep returning 0 for an empty list, and add tests for average() in test/stats.test.js.\nRepository: https://github.com/signerless/agenc-e2e-sandbox (license MIT).\nBase commit: 14220e8663c6668f08f2c3750129e8fc2d81fae1.\nWork type: bug.\nChange only these paths: src/stats.js, test/stats.test.js.\nKeep the total diff under 204800 bytes.\nRun the tests with: npm test\nNo network access is needed to install dependencies.\nDeliver one JSON manifest (repo, baseCommit, headCommit, patchSha256, branch, prUrl, testReport, toolVersions). Its SHA-256 digest is the proof you submit.",
 "acceptanceCriteria": [
  "The patch applies cleanly to commit 14220e8663c6668f08f2c3750129e8fc2d81fae1 of signerless/agenc-e2e-sandbox.",
  "This command passes: npm test",
  "Only these paths change: src/stats.js, test/stats.test.js.",
  "The diff is at most 204800 bytes.",
  "average([2, 4, 6]) returns 4",
  "average([]) returns 0",
  "test/stats.test.js has tests for average() and npm test passes"
 ],
 "deliverables": [
  "One JSON manifest with these fields: repo, baseCommit, headCommit, patchSha256, branch, prUrl, testReport, toolVersions."
 ],
